cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Forest Lab: Forest growth, ecological succession and anthropogenic interference"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23859145
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23859145"
date-released: 2026-11-01
authors:
  - family-names: Sales
    given-names: Jomil Costa Abreu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8722-8398"
abstract: >-
  Forest Lab is an interactive 3D simulator of tropical forest succession over
  1,000 years on a 100-hectare landscape. It covers five succession phases and
  five functional groups, natural (riparian) and anthropogenic (vineyard/agriculture,
  urban) edge effects, gap dynamics, rainfall and soil fertility drivers,
  aboveground biomass estimates, and an emulated high-density airborne LiDAR
  point cloud. The interface is available in English and Portuguese.
keywords:
  - ecological succession
  - tropical forest
  - edge effect
  - forest regeneration
  - riparian forest
  - LiDAR
  - aboveground biomass
  - 3D simulation
  - environmental education
